**One knob: yes. One ramp: no.** The four spacing systems collapse to a single unitless `--size` knob and three clamps -- but not to one ramp. Measured over the 20 spacing-audit pages at 400/1280/1920/3440, the candidate injected as an unlayered stylesheet; `framework.css` untouched.

![the study page](study.jpg)

**[The study page](/imagine/design/size/)** -- drag the box, watch pad, gap and rhythm follow it while the reading text never moves; the eight lines; the before/after table. Detail one click down on the page: [what was refuted](/imagine/design/size/alternatives.md) and [what lands if approved](/imagine/design/size/landing.md).

The standard, eight lines:

```css
:root { --size: 1 }

:where(*) {
    --pad:  calc(clamp(1em, 2.6% - 1.1em,   4em)   * var(--size));
    --gap:  calc(clamp(1em, 1.5cqi - 0.3em, 2.6em) * var(--size));
    --flow: calc(clamp(2em, 1.4cqi + 0.8em, 3em)   * var(--size));
}

.size-small { --size: 0.75 }  .size-regular { --size: 1 }  .size-large { --size: 1.25 }
```

**The numbers** (median pad / gap / rhythm over 20 pages):
- at 1280 -- today 5.4 / 7.9 / 28.8px; the candidate 5.4 / 7.9 / 28.8px; one ramp 5.4 / 6.0 / **13.5**px
- at 3440 -- today 6.5 / 22.1 / 48.6px; the candidate 6.5 / 20.8 / 48.6px; one ramp 6.5 / 20.7 / 49.3px

**Four findings.** (1) One ramp with fixed multipliers is refuted: padding grows 5.0x across 400-3440 and rhythm 1.9x, so tuning to 3440 halves the paragraph rhythm at 1280. (2) `--size` must be unitless, not the literal `.75em` -- an em can only move a clamp's floor and cap, so at 1280 the em form moves rhythm 0% where unitless moves it 25%. (3) Type stays viewport-only: three containers deep at 3440 the text reads 18/18/18px under the candidate and 18/17.5/**12**px if type took `cqi`; display type is the one allowed exception. (4) The columns host is not a fourth system -- its `--page-column-pad-x` and the candidate's `--pad` measure within 2.6% of each other in the same box.

**If it lands: 945 renames** by grep (829 ramp names, 103 default names, 6 `--spacing` reads, 7 level classes) plus 18 column-token sites. Two behaviour changes hide inside: the level word starts reaching the 650 component gaps that read the un-levelled `--gap-ramp` (today `spacing-tight` leaves the 3440 median gap unmoved at 25.3px; the candidate takes it to 19.0px), and `vw` becomes `cqi`, which is identical on a plain page and container-aware inside a column, frame or rail.

**Two calls for the owner**, both on the study page: the ladder (0.75/1/1.25 as briefed, against the 09-05 decision's more visible 0.6/1/1.6), and aliases-or-sweep.

**Left, with reasons.** Nothing applied -- `framework.css` waits on slice 1's byte-identical proof, by the mastermind's order. `styles/css-scopes.txt` needs a `size-` line when the standard lands; outside today's fence. The drag edge hides under 34em of screen (ext/grip's own rule) -- the level chips work there.
